  "query_preview": "Pattern & Climate Outlook (This Weekend through Mid-\nOctober):\nConfidence is high (80-90%) that a robust upper-level ridge will \nbuild over the Northern Rockies this weekend and persist into next\nweek.\n\n   -Daytime Temperatures: Anomalously warm air aloft (10-20\n    degrees F above normal at 850mb) will translate to mild days,\n    though valley inversions may cap maximum warming potential in\n    lower elevations.\n\n   -Overnight Temperatures: Valley lows will trend cooler than \n    standard NBM guidance due to strong radiational cooling (clear\n    skies, light winds, dry air). Mid-slopes and thermal belts \n    will remain significantly warmer and drier overnight.\n\n   -Long-Range Trend: Ensemble clusters and CPC outlooks favor a\n    extended period of warmer and drier-than-normal conditions\n    through mid-October. Brief, minor disturbances remain\n    possible, but no significant precipitation events are \n    indicated.",
